# Next.js Technical SEO Optimizer

When asked to "optimize for SEO", "fix meta tags", "add structured data", or "run seo optimizer -all":

## 1. Scanner Commands
- Run `npm run seo:scan` (or `node scripts/seo-scan.mjs`) to audit all 25 routes.

## 2. Core SEO Requirements
- **Single `<h1>`:** Exactly one semantic `<h1>` tag per page.
- **Dedicated Metadata:** Every route has dedicated metadata or an adjacent `layout.tsx` exporting metadata via `buildPageMetadata` from `@/app/lib/seo`.
- **JSON-LD Structured Data:** Ensure Schema.org structured data (`<StructuredData data={[...]} />`) is present.
- **Image Attributes:** All `<Image>` components have descriptive `alt` text; above-the-fold hero images include `priority={true}`.
- **Open Graph:** Define `ogImage`, `ogAlt`, and `siteName`.
- **Verification:** Always verify with `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npm run seo:scan`.
